# Ruff on every Python change

Ship Python that already matches CI. After editing any `.py` file, and again
before committing, opening a pull request, or reporting work complete, run ruff
on every changed file. Tests passing is not enough — `ruff check` is not
`ruff format --check`.

```bash
uv run ruff format <changed.py> ...
uv run ruff check <changed.py> ...
```

CI (`lint` job) runs the same tools across the tree:

```bash
uv run ruff check .
uv run ruff format --check .
```

- Format **and** check. Fix findings, rerun until both pass, then include those
  files in the same commit.
- Prefer ruff's quote style (single quotes when the string contains `"`).
- Mention in the user update that ruff format and check passed (or what you
  fixed).
